 ### Adaptive Interpolation for Isosurface Detection
-Adaptive Interpolation for Isosurface Detection interpolates input volume along rays at a predetermined sampling rate. It uses non-binary classifiers to adjust the acceptable density range for an isovalue surface based on data change rate [S2, unofficial]. When data values change slowly, a narrow range of acceptable values is used for the isovalue surface. When data values change rapidly, a wide range is used to avoid missing the surface [S2, unofficial]. It supports user selection of interpolation: nearest-neighbor (preview), linear (day-to-day), cubic (publication-quality) [S2, unofficial].
